From ef17832e677ae10eb4d9ee18a55007291df6cea7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 11:08:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 911/913] clk: stm32: fix panic after calibration failure

Fix calibration startup handling by removing trim ramp reconstruction,
which can introduce too high frequency variations.

Fix the calibration search logic by not stopping as soon as the next
trim value fails to improve the frequency, since forbidden trim values
may otherwise hide the best valid setting.
This also avoids ending up in the case where we think we found the
best trim, but it is actually out of range.

Fix CSI trim value handling on STM32MP1 (trim values are unsigned).

As part of these fixes, share the oscillator calibration algorithm
between STM32MP1 and STM32MP2.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git a8fdb447bb828cc100f2db01c38ad3c5008e43f4 clk: stm32: fix panic after calibration failure]
Change-Id: Idead171ab37de2bf2fdac378f27590eb497007e3
Signed-off-by: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/616745
